      "side": 1,
      "message": "small nit: compared to the previous version, we now have two Log.e() statements instead of one in case that `sendMessage()` or `recvMessage()` throws an exception.\n\nI think it would be cleaner to keep the catch block in the caller and mark this function as throwing both ErrnoException and InterrupedIOException, with no log statement. This way you can still log the full exception info on the caller side with more info (like the rtnl msg type or full request), and you can just have a `try finally` without a `catch` here to close the socket.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 509,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 509,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "5297564f_3629aad0",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
          "replacements": [
            {
              "path": "staticlibs/device/com/android/net/module/util/netlink/NetlinkUtils.java",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 508,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 510,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "        } catch (ErrnoException e) {\n            Log.e(TAG, \"Failed to send netlink message to get link information\", e);\n            return null;\n        } catch (InterruptedIOException e) {\n            Log.e(TAG, \"Failed to receive netlink message to get link information\", e);\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
